A||||5||Coupe'N||WS6 suspension VERSUS Sport/Lowering suspension...||||5||
Z||000000||Coupe'N||06-24-2001||05:34 PM||||Hey everyone, I took the struts, front sway bar, and front coils off my 84 SE which has the WS6 suspension package. I planned on putting them on my 87 coupe which has a rather soft type suspension.<BR>BUT, I was thinking though... If I bought the sport/lowering suspension products (i.e. koni's, KYB, Helliweg), what kind of improvements would this be over the WS6 suspension?<BR>Also, if I were to buy factory replacement spring/struts from the local auto parts store, how would they know if my fiero had the WS6 or not??? Would they give me the right suspension product?? or not??<BR>Thanks for any help on these questions.<P>Coupe'N outt!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||06-25-2001||09:20 PM||||You need the front AND rear springs. they are a matched set. You don't want to reuse those old struts. just the springs.<P>Don't worry about the WS6 when buying new shox/struts. Any shox/strut you buy today will out perform those made in 84 or 87. You can get KYB shox/struts for the OE setup.<P>The WS 6 springs are stiffer. just how much depends on what spring code they are. The info on that is in another thread.<P>If you take the Ws 6 springs and put them with new shox/struts then you should have a really decent handling car for rather cheap.<P>If 84 ws6 had the rear sway, you'll want to move that to. (Front maybe.. I'm told all the front bars are the same.)<BR><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||06-26-2001||02:19 AM||||The only Fiero's to have a rear sway bar stock were the 88 GT's and Forumla's. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Coupe'N||06-26-2001||07:00 PM||||Thanks for the info guys! I have one more question though... would the aftermarket lowering/sport spings have a better effect with the aftermarket shocks and struts, than the WS6 springs with the aftermarket struts and shocks?<BR>Ohh by the way.. I have the stiffest springs offered in 84'... 6MN,7MN,8WY,9WY.<BR>Thanks for the help, and info!<P>Coupe'N outt!!!||||reg||6
Z||000004||theogre||06-26-2001||08:06 PM||||I have and 87SC. my suspension is the second stiffest of the "regular" list. I don't think I could take it any stiffer than it is and I still need new struts.<P>In all seriousness... I'd go with those springs and new shox/struts. It will make a hell of an improvement without the problems lowering causes.<P>If you chose new wheel/tires carefully you'll create an optical illusion of being lower than you really are. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||BAM-BAM||06-26-2001||08:35 PM|||| Yes, if you put or Eibach or ST lowering springs on with the KYB's or Koni's. You will absolutely blow the WS6 out of the water. Some say it's to harsh, I like mine just fine. I have Eibach ProKit springs and KYB's with polys and it is an awesome set up. You will enjoy it far more than any stock set up, even the 88 stock set up can't compare.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
